Public keys that sign Baseline agent releases (docs/agent.md §5.2).

Every agent is built with this file and installs only updates signed by one
of these keys. The private keys are the RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY secret of the
repository's "release" environment on GitHub; the server never has them.
At most two keys: the current one and, while rotating, the next. Add one
with

    openssl pkey -in release.key -pubout >> internal/pki/release-keys.pem

-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
MCowBQYDK2VwAyEAvk1skNcpLmRD7jJP6as+9iOAKL8onhPdawB+id5C11k=
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
